Introduction
============

This tool provides a Python interface to LIBLINEAR for incremental and
decremental learning.


Examples
========

matlab> [label, instance] = libsvmread('../heart_scale');
matlab> wsmodel = train(label, instance, '-s 2');
matlab> save('model.mat', 'wsmodel');

matlab> load('model.mat');
matlab> [label, instance] = libsvmread('../heart_scale');
matlab> model = train(label, instance, '-s 2 -i wsmodel');


>>> import scipy
>>> from liblinear.liblinearutil import *

>>> y, x = svm_read_problem('../heart_scale', return_scipy = True) # y: ndarray, x: csr_matrix
>>> m = train(y, x, '-s 2')
>>> save_model('heart_scale.model', m)

# Use -i to load the model saved earlier for continuous training

>>> m = train(y, x, '-s 2 -e 0.0001 -i heart_scale.model')

